# inc-5v5l: does Dispel Evil's +4/+6 deflection bonus (component 0, xval
# TRAP_EVENT, yval EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE)) actually apply on a REAL attack, not
# just get read from code?
#
# THE SCENE. A fresh orc priest of Aiswin (chargen-priest.keys) turns on
# Infinite Mana only (Wizard Mode Switches row 8 -- src/Tables.cpp's Wizard
# Options list: Cheat Death, Auto-Identify Items, Free Advancement, Infinite
# Fatigue, Always Rest Safely, Ignore Spell Failure, Know All Spells,
# Infinite Mana is the 8th), so casting the level-5, 16-mana spell is never
# refused for mana. Learns Dispel Evil through Learn Any Spell and casts it
# -- no Free Advancement, because the deflection bonus is a flat +4/+6, not
# scaled by caster level. Freeze Monsters is left OFF on purpose: a summoned
# goblin one square east (RIGHT ENTER, adjacent) is hostile and, left
# unfrozen, attacks the caster on its own turn. '.' (Wait One Turn) lets it
# act three times, which is more than enough for one goblin turn.
#
# THE ORACLE is the game's own combat-roll line, already stored in the
# message log because OPT_STORE_ROLLS is on in tools/gates/Options.Dat
# (src/Fight.cpp:9831-9836 prints "Attack: 1d20 (n) ... vs. Def [<breakdown>
# = N][hit/miss]", and the handler's own e.strDef append -- src/Fight.cpp's
# generic breakdown, this spell's own " +N DispEv" -- lands inside that
# bracket). tools/check_dispel_evil.sh pages the whole log ('v', PGUP*100,
# then PGDN) and greps for "DispEv" in an "Attack:" line. The goblin is the
# only creature in the scene that can attack the caster, so any such line is
# unambiguous.

@include chargen-priest.keys
ESC
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*7
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Dispel Evil" ENTER
@dump:learned

m
@choose "Dispel Evil"
@dump:after-cast

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:goblin-summoned

.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-wait-1
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-wait-2
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-wait-3

v
@dump:messages-bottom
PGUP*100
@dump:messages-top
PGDN*1
@dump:messages-mid1
PGDN*1
@dump:messages-mid2
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
